     1	// THE HOLDER'S SIGN OF LIFE (docs/PRINCIPLES.md).
     2	// A work step is the work: it may legitimately run for hours, and while it does
     3	// the item goes dark and the executing leash cannot tell it from a dead runner.
     4	// So the executor comments on its own item at a fixed interval, and the scheduler run's
     5	// reclaim measures silence from THAT rather than from a run-length cap.
     6	//
     7	// One mechanism, two things it buys: long work becomes legal (the run cap that
     8	// held the leash arithmetic together retires), and the item's timeline stays live
     9	// through work nobody can otherwise see.
    10	//
    11	// WHAT COUNTS AS ACTIVITY IS THE HOLDER'S OWN SIGNAL, never the issue's
    12	// `updated_at` (#924). Any comment moves `updated_at` — including one written by
    13	// an executor that LOST the claim race and let go — so a clock read off the issue
    14	// defers the reclaim of an item nobody is working on. The struck claims a lost
    15	// race leaves behind carry the episode marker, and are excluded here for exactly
    16	// that reason.
    17	
    18	import { nowMs } from '../world/clock.mjs';
    19	
    20	import { CLAIM_MARKER, EPISODE_MARKER, PROGRESS_HEADING } from '../../public/task-constants.mjs';
    21	import { parseProgressLines, withSection } from '../../public/work-item-grammar.mjs';
    22	
    23	export const HEARTBEAT_MARKER = '<!-- claudinite-heartbeat -->';
    24	
    25	// Comfortably inside the executing leash (60m), so a live holder is never
    26	// reclaimed on a single missed beat: it takes four in a row.
